{"at": "2026-11-23T19:09:35.764267+00:00", "event_id": "01M84X0K4MA99F8Y990Q2GCTK1", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M84X0K4K462YEMYV9RHB5T96", "input_key": "generated_page_sequencing", "mission_id": "01M84X07GSZS94MXX0RYYNMBJK", "mission_slug": "subprocessor-catalog-01M84X07", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["Split into a later WP gated on #359 (recommended)", "Build provisionally now against #359 draft", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "Issue #359 (generated-section contract) is still open. How should this mission handle the generated sub-processor list page? (1) Split it into a final WP that waits on #359 being accepted, while the catalog, validation, agent API, change feed, tom_classification link and docs ship independently. (2) Build it now following #359's drafted contract (generated: {by, at, source_digest} stamp plus a --check drift gate), clearly marked provisional in ADR-0085 and on the page.", "recorded_at": "2026-11-23T19:09:35.764267Z", "run_id": "01M84X0K4K462YEMYV9RHB5T96", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-23T19:09:35.763740Z", "step_id": "specify.scope.generated-page-sequencing"}}
{"at": "2026-11-23T20:56:29.363338+00:00", "event_id": "01M8534ADKR0HZDXEWPTQE56ES", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M84X0K4K462YEMYV9RHB5T96", "final_answer": "Split into a later WP gated on #359 (recommended). Decider: operator (answered 'go', relayed by dispatcher 2026-11-23). Final WP builds on ADR-0087 (PR #445; Proposed on GitHub at time of recording) once it is accepted and merged.", "mission_id": "01M84X07GSZS94MXX0RYYNMBJK", "mission_slug": "subprocessor-catalog-01M84X07", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": false, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-11-23T20:56:29.363338Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M84X0K4K462YEMYV9RHB5T96", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-23T20:56:29.362348Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
{"at": "2026-11-23T20:56:57.734325+00:00", "event_id": "01M8535646EYAH7SEQ76GTAB64", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M8535645HETHAQ432516SAAY", "input_key": "change_feed_shape", "mission_id": "01M84X07GSZS94MXX0RYYNMBJK", "mission_slug": "subprocessor-catalog-01M84X07", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["A: dedicated RSS + JSON changes from since/until (recommended)", "B: from changelog fragments", "C: JSON only, RSS later", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "With the generated page deferred, what is the sub-processor change feed? (A) A dedicated RSS feed (subprocessors.xml), one item per addition (since) and per removal (until), plus the same entries as a changes list in api/subprocessors.json. Derived only from since/until, and carrying dates rather than a build-time 'current/upcoming' status so builds stay byte-stable. A future-dated since or until is how a site gives advance notice. (B) The same, but entries come from changelog fragments instead of since/until. (C) Only the JSON changes list in the agent API, with no RSS feed until the page WP.", "recorded_at": "2026-11-23T20:56:57.734325Z", "run_id": "01M8535645HETHAQ432516SAAY", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-23T20:56:57.733225Z", "step_id": "specify.feed.change-feed-shape"}}
{"at": "2026-11-23T21:05:42.191823+00:00", "event_id": "01M853N69FV6KP3ECBWHQ0983Q", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M8535645HETHAQ432516SAAY", "final_answer": "A: dedicated RSS feed subprocessors.xml (one item per since=added, per until=removed) plus the same entries as 'changes' in api/subprocessors.json; derived only from since/until; dates only, no build-time status (byte-stable); a future-dated since/until is the advance-notice mechanism. Decider: operator ('2A', relayed verbatim by dispatcher 2026-11-23).", "mission_id": "01M84X07GSZS94MXX0RYYNMBJK", "mission_slug": "subprocessor-catalog-01M84X07", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": false, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-11-23T21:05:42.191823Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M8535645HETHAQ432516SAAY", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-23T21:05:42.190796Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
{"at": "2026-11-23T21:05:58.357566+00:00", "event_id": "01M853NP2NS8SYVRVNQ7TF3TR6", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M853NP2MPP7HNWKMX9K8Y2ST", "input_key": "record_field_set", "mission_id": "01M84X07GSZS94MXX0RYYNMBJK", "mission_slug": "subprocessor-catalog-01M84X07", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["A: ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 list + optional location_note (recommended)", "B: free text", "C: free text now, structured later", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "Record field set (\u2696 counsel reviews it before it is called DPA-ready). Fields as in the issue: { id, name, address?, contact?, processing, location, responsibilities, since, until?, external_references?, tom_classification? }. external_references reuses the existing page shape (inline or {type: biblio, id}), and tom_classification reuses the page field shape from ADR-0080. Open point: how is  typed? (A) A non-empty list of ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes (e.g. [DE, US]) with an optional free-text location_note. Machine-checkable, useful later for transfer analysis. (B) Free text. (C) Free text now, structured later. No transfer-mechanism field in any case; that is a follow-up issue.", "recorded_at": "2026-11-23T21:05:58.357566Z", "run_id": "01M853NP2MPP7HNWKMX9K8Y2ST", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-23T21:05:58.356510Z", "step_id": "specify.entities.record-field-set"}}
{"at": "2026-11-23T21:10:16.592474+00:00", "event_id": "01M853XJ8GGHMJ9HTXRQM227H1", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M853NP2MPP7HNWKMX9K8Y2ST", "final_answer": "A: location is a non-empty list of ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes plus an optional free-text location_note; transfer-mechanism field out of scope (follow-up issue). (Question text lost the word 'location' to a shell-quoting slip; the question was how 'location' is typed.) Decider: operator ('1A', relayed verbatim by dispatcher 2026-11-23, mapped by dispatcher to option A of this DM).", "mission_id": "01M84X07GSZS94MXX0RYYNMBJK", "mission_slug": "subprocessor-catalog-01M84X07", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": false, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-11-23T21:10:16.592474Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M853NP2MPP7HNWKMX9K8Y2ST", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-23T21:10:16.591525Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
