{"at": "2026-11-23T21:14:51.358559+00:00", "event_id": "01M8545YJYZG8S0WYK8D3SY1TT", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M8545YJX3DY4G3DEYX81G49Y", "input_key": "build_failure_point", "mission_id": "01M84X07GSZS94MXX0RYYNMBJK", "mission_slug": "subprocessor-catalog-01M84X07", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["A: fail at config setup in a file-gated integration (recommended)", "B: fail when the route renders", "Other"], "origin_flow": "plan", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "PLAN", "question": "Where does an invalid sub-processor catalog fail the build? (A) In a new doc-kitty:subprocessors integration at astro:config:setup. It reads the file once, validates it with the shared bare-Node core (the same core validate-catalog.mjs imports) against the bibliography and measures catalogs, and throws one aggregate error before any page renders. It injects /api/subprocessors.json and /subprocessors.xml only when the file exists (gherkin precedent), so served-surface detection drives the api/index.json links. (B) Lazily, when the routes render. Simpler, but the error comes late and a missing route cannot be told apart from a failed one.", "recorded_at": "2026-11-23T21:14:51.358559Z", "run_id": "01M8545YJX3DY4G3DEYX81G49Y", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-23T21:14:51.357253Z", "step_id": "plan.architecture.build-failure-point"}}
{"at": "2026-11-23T22:25:56.652742+00:00", "event_id": "01M85883XCZP3PV1TF9N09RFJD", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M8545YJX3DY4G3DEYX81G49Y", "final_answer": "A: fail at astro:config:setup in a new file-gated doc-kitty:subprocessors integration; validate once with the shared bare-Node core; one aggregate error before rendering; routes injected only when the file exists. Engineering alignment confirmed as written (pure core + bare-Node loader, bibliography/measures ids passed in, embedded ISO alpha-2 list, RSS reuses rss.ts helpers, WP01-WP05 with WP05 gated on #445). Decider: operator ('as recommended', relayed verbatim by dispatcher 2026-11-23).", "mission_id": "01M84X07GSZS94MXX0RYYNMBJK", "mission_slug": "subprocessor-catalog-01M84X07", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": false, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-11-23T22:25:56.652742Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M8545YJX3DY4G3DEYX81G49Y", "state_entered_at": "2026-11-23T22:25:56.651434Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
